Description: Look for ANGLE libraries in cef/ subdirectory on Linux
 On Debian, CEF's ANGLE libraries (libEGL.so, libGLESv2.so) are installed in
 /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/cef/ subdirectory to avoid conflicts with system
 GLVND/Mesa libraries at /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/.
 .
 Without this patch, CEF looks for ANGLE in the same directory as libcef.so
 (DIR_MODULE), which on Debian is /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/.
 This causes CEF to find the system GLVND loader instead of ANGLE, resulting
 in EGL_BAD_ATTRIBUTE errors because Mesa doesn't support some EGL attributes
 that CEF requires (e.g., EGL_CONTEXT_OPENGL_NO_ERROR_KHR).
 .
 The DIR_EXE/DIR_MODULE to DIR_ASSETS changes are already handled by the
 Debian Chromium patches (linux_assets_path_1936.patch). This patch only
 adds the cef/ subdirectory lookup for ANGLE libraries in egl_util.cc.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <juan.mendezr@proton.me>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-02-16

diff --git a/ui/ozone/common/egl_util.cc b/ui/ozone/common/egl_util.cc
index 63a2305..69a7d86 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/common/egl_util.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/common/egl_util.cc
@@ -151,6 +151,11 @@ bool LoadDefaultEGLGLES2Bindings(
 #if !BUILDFLAG(IS_FUCHSIA)
     if (!base::PathService::Get(base::DIR_ASSETS, &module_path))
       return false;
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
+    // Debian: ANGLE libraries are installed in cef/ subdirectory to avoid
+    // conflicts with system GLVND/Mesa libraries at /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/
+    module_path = module_path.Append(FILE_PATH_LITERAL("cef"));
+#endif
 #endif

     glesv2_path = module_path.Append(kAngleGlesSoname);
